<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kerbogha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1102</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kerbogha was a Turkish commander who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> as atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>. In 1098 he led a large Muslim army to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>, but the crusaders, who had just taken the city, defeated him outside its walls in June 1098. He kept Mosul until his death in 1102.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kerbogha.jpg" alt="Kerbogha" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kerbogha_Antiochie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
